Qualify a supplier through the material and route they actually control (@cs-supplier: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY", #source "../sources/Chemical-Supply-Resilience-EPA.lingua#r_2NVE96BRQ8Q3WYFP2ZQ3NTE11F", #source "../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME", #chemical-supply-systems "Receive-a-physical-delivery-before-releasing-a-material.lingua#r_6TX7C86D26AMZDW2V07MYVJ8NZ") { r_61RKSTFXH4ZXAD0069T2SCMM6X
**Read:** [Good trade and distribution practices for pharmaceutical starting materials — WHO](../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY), the entire procurement, quality, documentation and contract discussion; [Supply Chain Resilience: Guide for Water and Wastewater Utilities — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Resilience-EPA.lingua#r_2NVE96BRQ8Q3WYFP2ZQ3NTE11F), the complete supplier-management section and cases; [Caustic Soda Handbook — OxyChem](../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME), the complete actual grade and analytical-method evidence for the chosen comparison.

List the claims needed to accept a source: product identity/function, consistent quality, representative evidence, packaging/transport capability, continuity and communication of changes. Identify whether the organisation manufactures, obtains, blends, repacks or merely sells the material. A supplier list does not show how many independent production routes are available.

Build a qualification study for one chemical using actual public product and method documents. Compare initial evaluation, a small documented trial, repeated deliveries and continuing performance. Separate a producer's capability from a distributor's control over the downstream history. Ask how the proposed supplier learns of an upstream source change and how that information reaches the user.

Evaluate two plausible sources on the same intended-use requirement and disclose missing evidence. Certificates, audits and accreditation have scopes; determine what the particular evidence covers rather than ranking suppliers by the presence of a logo. Include analytical turnaround and technical support, minimum campaign quantities, maintenance and alternative supply arrangements. Later advanced studies should defend an evidence-based decision and describe how it changes when a product, route, contact material or user process changes. Literature-only work should state which supplier claims remain untested.

**Continue:** [Connect receiving observations to the material that will be used](Receive-a-physical-delivery-before-releasing-a-material.lingua#r_6TX7C86D26AMZDW2V07MYVJ8NZ).

